uffers from dissociative identity  disorder so when he goes from one  character to another the character that  he becomes cannot remember anything that  the previous character did also at the  same time he is enslaved by the egyptian  god konchu and in this article by usa  today oscar isaac actually gives us a  lot of information about his alternate  personalities and actually quite a bit  of details about the plot of moon knight  so let's go ahead and break that down  the article starts off by saying the new  six episode disney plus series  introduces isaac as a supernatural  vigilante and two-fisted avatar of the  egyptian deity khonshu with several  other sides surfacing due to  dissociative identity disorder there's  american mercenary mark spectre  why did you call me mark british gift  shop employee stephen grant caped  crusader moon knight and the mysterious  suitclad mr knight and usa today goes on  to say that and those are just the  personalities we can mention before the  show starts meaning there are actually  going to be several more personalities  that we see mark spector have in the  comics mark spector is kind of the  original person that is moon knight and  even in this interview one of the  executive producers grant curtis says  that this is the journey of mark spector  he says it's a story about identity and  finding one's true self the journey that  mark spector is on during our whole show  is who am i and how do i reconcile  portions of my past present and  potential future that i don't  necessarily agree with coming to terms  with our baggage and learning to live  with ourselves is what we all deal with  on a day-to-day basis so although this  is indeed going to be a very  supernatural show dealing with egyptian  gods and such which we're about to talk  about but it's also going to be kind of  realistic in the fact that they're going  to address very realistic things like  mental health while at the same time  this is going to be a kind of dark show  and apparently he's going to be meeting  some other worldly beings now we know  he's going to be meeting konchu but  perhaps there's going to be more the  article says steven suffers from random  blackouts voices in his head and trouble  distinguishing between his waking and  dream lives with flashing visions of  egyptian relics and memories that aren't  his own he stumbles into some dangerous  otherworldly dealings and meets mark  creating an initial tension between the  two personalities with different goals  and objectives so in this trailer and in  the very first trailer that we got for  moon knight we see who is actually  stephen pick up the phone and somebody  addresses him by the name mark and he  says why did you call me mark now again  mark is the original who comes in  contact with konchu the egyptian god and  since he says that he has flashbacks of  egyptian relics and voices in his head  i'm assuming those are the memories and  flashbacks of mark or they actually  could be the memories of the egyptian  god khan shu because konchu uses mark as  his avatar in this world and we'll get  to that story in just a bit but oscar  isaac actually describes the differences  between stephen grant and mark spector  here in this article he says viewers  first meet stephen an english bloke who  is a bit confused and doesn't have great  social skills and says the wrong things  at the wrong times and is completely  sincere he's also someone longing for a  connection and in a way could be the  counterpoint to the classic tortured  dark vigilante guy we've seen a lot but  then he says with mark spector i leaned  into this chicago guy who pushes people  away you feel the way steven feels why  is he such a jerk i don't really want to  be around him as the story progresses  you see that happen so not only is mark  spector steven grant all of the  different identities going to have all  of the different identities but they're  not going to get along with each other  in fact oscar isaac said that it was  important that the series feels  experimental for audience members and  quite true to the psychological horror  of not knowing what's happening and the  slow revelations of the truth and we can  definitely see that in some parts of  this trailer with the god konshu now  there are actually several new scenes of  khanshu in this trailer and each scene  with konshu is pretty intense and kind  of scary it looks like mark slash steven  slash whoever he is at the time is  always running away from him and kanchi  was always kind of chasing him so big  horror vibes there but what i think  they're going to be exploring is whether  or not mark spector can actually tell if  konchu is real or fake in the comics  even moon knight himself doubts it  sometimes he doesn't really know and no  one else really believes him as well  they just think he's crazy originally  mark spector was a mercenary he was a  former marine and he was former cia but  as a mercenary he took a job in sudan  where a fellow mercenary bushman killed  an archaeologist  mark was appalled at this behavior and  he actually saved the archaeologist's  daughter marlene who we believe is  actually going to be the character leila  in the show marlene would eventually go  on to become his lover and the mother of  his daughter but mark stood up to  bushmen in which bushman practically  killed him he fatally wounded him and  mark crawled away he crawls away to a  tomb and he actually dies but he dies in  front of a statue of the egyptian moon  god konchu he dies but he is suddenly  then revived and fully healed and he  claims that konchu wants him to be his  moon knight and he wants him to redeem  his life of violence and protect and  avenge the innocent now for a long time  it's not known if kanchu is actually  real or is simply made up by mark  spector in his mind but eventually it is  revealed that konchu is indeed real and  he's one of several entities from a  place called the other void a dimension  outside of normal time and space and  these people were worshiped as gods by  ancient earth people so if they stay  true to this fact in the comics the  consu that we see here is indeed real  and we actually see one particular scene  towards the end of this trailer where it  looks like konchi was doing something  pretty big perhaps showing mark the  world where he comes from or perhaps  this is some type of an attack some type  of a defense or perhaps just a vision  but what looks like is happening here in  this trailer in the first trailer is  that steven grant and the other  personalities have kind of repressed the  mark spectre personality because mark  specter is the one who is originally  contacted and resurrected essentially by  konchu and that's why steven grant has  all of these memories of ancient egypt  egyptian relics but he doesn't know  where they're from because it's mark's  memories and they've repressed them and  as far as ethan hawke's villain goes we  don't really know that much about him  yet but it does look like he's leading  somewhat of a cult so i'm assuming that  he is searching for the ancient god  konchu as well and realizes that mark  spector might actually be the avatar for  konchu which is why we can see oscar  isaac in egypt at some points in this  trailer and a lot of people are actually  surrounding him and it does look like  he's kind of there against his will and  could be a prisoner this could be ethan  huck's villain and their cult kidnapping  him taking him to konchu's statue and  perhaps trying to offer him as some sort  of a sacrifice to the god whatever it  may be this trailer looks fantastic and  the story of moon knight is apparently  going to be pretty epic a dark  supernatural show that is going to focus  on mental illness it's going to be  pretty great but let me know what you  think about this in the comments down  below don't forget to like the video and  subscribe so you don't miss out on  future mcu videos for live updates you  can follow me on instagram or twitter  and as always thank you all so much for  watching woof

